<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ's Turners &amp; Growers in contract to sell carpark.</title>
<headline>NZ's Turners &amp; Growers in contract to sell carpark.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand's Turners and Growers Ltd said on Tuesday it had entered into an unconditional contract to dispose of its Fanshawe Street carpark for NZ$5.65 million.</p>
<p>The contract would be settled during the course of the next financial year.</p>
<p>Earlier, the company reported a year net profit of NZ$383,000, against last year's loss of NZ$446,000.</p>
</text>
